# REQUIRES: python-api
# A part of a Python simulation whose constraints fail raises SimulationError
# with the step and the set, keeps the state from before the part, and
# leaves the process able to run another simulation
# (D[constraint-failure-stop]), scenario constraints of
# Inputs/python_position_guard.py: the hydrogen of the first amide of the
# dipeptide starts at 100 nm/ps, and its group of SHAKE fails in the first
# step, in double and mixed precision.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_position_guard.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU constraints | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: constraints Double: fails after step 0 and keeps its state; another simulation runs: the constraints of the set 'shake1' failed at step 1: a constrained length is off its target or is not a number
# CHECK: constraints Mixed: fails after step 0 and keeps its state; another simulation runs: the constraints of the set 'shake1' failed at step 1
# CHECK: position guard constraints passed
